id: pm-vcs-bisect-shallow-report
title: Preserve bisect reports when the culprit is a shallow boundary
description: "A bisect verdict whose first bad commit is a shallow merge parent cannot be enriched because linkedItems unconditionally reads the omitted first parent. Range construction succeeds, but manual bad and subsequent status return object_not_found. This is a separate provenance-reporting path discovered during PR 131 review round 3, beyond the requested ancestry and checkout fixes."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-19T22:37:30.807Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-19T23:25:30.096Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: A real shallow-merge regression covers bad/run/status when the first bad commit has an omitted parent; available explicit associations remain available; missing provenance has an honest omission or boundary receipt; complete-history and root-commit reports remain correct.
parent: pm-vcs-p7bisect
repro_steps: "Create an empty-tree ancestor A, good G with parent A, side S with parent A, and merge M with parents G and S. Clone M with depth 2 so A is absent and G/S are shallow. Initialize a real tracker and linked test in the clone. Start bisect G M, mark S bad, then request status."
expected_result: Keep the core bisect conclusion available and report unavailable file-derived attribution explicitly instead of throwing or inventing provenance.
actual_result: Start succeeds; marking S bad and later status both fail with No object for the omitted first-parent commit. The disposable reproduction verified the parent object is absent.
component: bisect
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-19T23:25:30.095Z",codex-agent,"Fixed in PR 131 review round: real depth-two merge clone verifies missing ancestor, manual bad plus status, automatic run plus status, explicit association deduplication/order, honest itemsBoundary=shallow, no hydration, restored HEAD and reset. Focused regression passes; reverting only linkedItems fails on missing parent. Related traceFile shallow-parent read fixed with an independent passing/reverting regression. Item remains in progress for orchestrator verification."
